WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:00.881
Hey guys, what's going on?

00:00:00.896 --> 00:00:01.761
It's me, Will Paterson.

00:00:01.786 --> 00:00:03.245
Welcome back to a new video.

00:00:03.308 --> 00:00:05.081
Today I'm going to show you
something different.

00:00:05.156 --> 00:00:07.773
I'm going to show you how you
can actually create mockups

00:00:07.784 --> 00:00:09.693
inside of Photoshop.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:14.009
This is a really basic way of
doing so, but really effective.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.824
So the first thing you want to
do is in Photoshop, we're going

00:00:19.836 --> 00:00:21.037
to bring in an image.

00:00:21.074 --> 00:00:22.797
I'm just going to bring in this one.

00:00:22.824 --> 00:00:23.761
This is a coffee mug.

00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:26.245
It's the easiest way to show you. 
Now when presenting to a

00:00:26.256 --> 00:00:27.909
client what I like to do.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.033
And many other designers, they
love to put their work on to

00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:33.441
products that mean something 
to the company.

00:00:33.516 --> 00:00:36.639
So, for instance, a coffee shop
would have a coffee logo on

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.169
their coffee cup if it's a
takeaway cup.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.833
But what if we have an image
like this, where it's just a

00:00:41.844 --> 00:00:46.245
static image and we need to make 
it look real with the logo on it.

00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:48.937
So bring your image and make
sure it's high quality so you

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.057
can tell by the way it zooms in.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.337
If it zooms in and it's nice
and crisp, that's good.

00:00:53.424 --> 00:00:56.185
First thing I'm going to do is
hold Alt or option and just

00:00:56.196 --> 00:00:57.601
double click on the background
layer.

00:00:57.626 --> 00:00:58.921
And I'm going to call this cup.

00:00:59.006 --> 00:01:00.453
There's a lot of things I could
do better.

00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:02.679
However, I'm going to show you
how to get the work onto the

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.065
cup face itself.

00:01:04.188 --> 00:01:05.737
So we're going to use a shape.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:08.185
So the first thing we need to
do is press U or go to the

00:01:08.196 --> 00:01:11.221
shape down here and just
approximately over the top of

00:01:11.232 --> 00:01:14.065
this, create a rectangle, make
sure it's overlapping.

00:01:14.138 --> 00:01:17.037
I'm going to change the colour
of the rectangle to any colour.

00:01:17.184 --> 00:01:19.681
And then right here, I'm going
to right click on this shape.

00:01:19.706 --> 00:01:21.261
And this is really important.

00:01:21.396 --> 00:01:23.733
Right click and go to Convert
to Smart Object.

00:01:23.832 --> 00:01:27.314
What this does is it allows us
to click into that shape layer

00:01:27.326 --> 00:01:30.333
or the smart object and edit it
in here.

00:01:30.432 --> 00:01:36.057
And when we save that, it will
apply it to anything in here.

00:01:36.144 --> 00:01:39.204
This also means we can warp
this rectangle into the shape

00:01:39.216 --> 00:01:42.237
of the coffee cup and it would
apply the effect.

00:01:42.384 --> 00:01:45.673
So on the smart object, we're
going to call this the edit.

00:01:45.782 --> 00:01:48.204
I'm going to change the opacity
to around 30 because I want to

00:01:48.216 --> 00:01:49.605
see the mug behind it.

00:01:49.668 --> 00:01:52.417
Press command T or control T
for free transform.

00:01:52.514 --> 00:01:53.421
And then go up here.

00:01:53.436 --> 00:01:54.837
You'll see this warp option.

00:01:54.924 --> 00:01:55.693
Click on warp.

00:01:55.742 --> 00:01:59.109
You'll automatically see this
mesh pop up here.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.995
Now this mesh is really cool
because what you can do is warp

00:02:02.006 --> 00:02:02.889
it around things.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.297
It's like a 3D mesh.

00:02:04.394 --> 00:02:07.653
What we're going to do is warp
it around the mug here.

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:09.249
There's plenty of ways to do this.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.845
In fact, you can actually go up
to the warp function up here

00:02:11.856 --> 00:02:14.325
and change the warp function here.

00:02:14.388 --> 00:02:16.677
It's got loads of presets, even
a cylinder one.

00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:19.209
But we're not going to use that
because it warps it a bit too much.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.365
We're just going to go to the default, 
the custom warp one up here.

00:02:23.436 --> 00:02:25.921
The first thing we want to do
is just approximately bring up

00:02:25.932 --> 00:02:29.353
the warp in the corners, like
so kind of matching the corners,

00:02:29.364 --> 00:02:32.953
not perfectly because we want
to have some overlap that

00:02:32.964 --> 00:02:33.969
we can edit later.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.201
Then we can just click on the
warp itself and just very

00:02:37.212 --> 00:02:38.913
carefully drag them in.

00:02:38.952 --> 00:02:41.925
It's going to look a bit strange at 
first, but we can always edit this.

00:02:41.988 --> 00:02:45.073
Then we can zoom in and start
messing around with these handles.

00:02:45.122 --> 00:02:47.973
It's kind of like the pen tool,
like the direct selection tool.

00:02:48.012 --> 00:02:51.477
But we're trying to get the warping 
to look nice all the way through.

00:02:51.564 --> 00:02:54.693
You can see why we change the
opacity here as well.

00:02:54.792 --> 00:02:57.249
If we zoom in, we can get as
fine as we want to.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.541
And I'm just going to kind of
eyeball this to make sure it

00:03:00.552 --> 00:03:02.961
works perfectly all the way through.

00:03:03.096 --> 00:03:05.787
and boom. Photoshop is a really 
powerful tool, so don't worry

00:03:05.798 --> 00:03:09.009
if you make any mistakes or if
it doesn't look perfect just yet.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.089
That's just the way it is.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.693
Okay, so now we have our warp
function.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.985
It kind of looks good so far.

00:03:15.048 --> 00:03:17.445
So press this button, appear to
apply it.

00:03:17.508 --> 00:03:19.261
We intentionally had some
overlap here because we're

00:03:19.272 --> 00:03:20.673
going to mask that out later.

00:03:20.712 --> 00:03:22.605
It's going to be a lot easier
for us to use.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.099
The next thing we're going to
do is go and change my fill,

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.553
my opacity to 100.

00:03:26.652 --> 00:03:28.237
Then we're going to change the
Blend mode.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:31.263
This is the huge part because
if we just have this shape on

00:03:31.274 --> 00:03:32.833
top, it kind of looks weird.

00:03:32.882 --> 00:03:34.069
It just looks flat.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.837
So the Blend mode option is
really important.

00:03:36.984 --> 00:03:38.241
On the smart object.

00:03:38.376 --> 00:03:40.549
Go to Blend mode and Linear
Burn.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.813
It might not look it right now,
but it'll actually help with

00:03:43.824 --> 00:03:46.093
creating the shadows and the
highlights.

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:48.879
It allows the highlights and
the shadows to appear through

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.169
so we don't have to do any
dodging or burning.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.673
It uses the shadows and the
highlights from the image.

00:03:54.722 --> 00:03:57.745
Now the problem we have is
obviously the colours of it strange.

00:03:57.818 --> 00:04:01.353
There's no work on it, but we
have the sharp corners down here.

00:04:01.452 --> 00:04:04.261
Now what I'm going to do is
hide this shape and we're going

00:04:04.272 --> 00:04:06.733
to select the coffee cup and
only the coffee cup.

00:04:06.782 --> 00:04:09.553
Now because we have a white
background on this, what I need

00:04:09.564 --> 00:04:12.625
to do is go to this object
selection tool up here and

00:04:12.636 --> 00:04:15.565
we're going to drag all the way
around it like so, and it will

00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:17.929
create a really nice quick selection.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:18.597
It's amazing.

00:04:18.684 --> 00:04:21.073
Then I'm going to press Command
C and Command V, which will

00:04:21.084 --> 00:04:25.213
paste only the object that I've
asked for it to paste, which is

00:04:25.224 --> 00:04:27.769
pretty neat. If you want to and
you want to get really precise

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.597
or the object tool doesn't it 
work for you, go ahead and

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.641
use the pen tool.

00:04:31.716 --> 00:04:33.085
I'm going to call this selection.

00:04:33.158 --> 00:04:35.005
I'm going to mark it as red,
because whenever I mark

00:04:35.016 --> 00:04:38.289
something as red, it means
don't touch it, don't use it.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:42.189
It's just for some nefarious
purpose, such as selecting it.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.989
The next thing we're going to
do is select the coffee cup.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.125
The reason why I've got it like
this is because I can just

00:04:47.136 --> 00:04:50.413
click like so with command onto
the shape and it will select

00:04:50.424 --> 00:04:52.105
the coffee cup automatically.

00:04:52.178 --> 00:04:55.509
What we want to do is get rid
of all these lines here.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:58.593
And the way we do that is just
by pressing it and masking it.

00:04:58.632 --> 00:05:01.065
We've applied a mask on top of
this.

00:05:01.128 --> 00:05:04.117
Now there's a few more problems,
but don't worry, you can see

00:05:04.128 --> 00:05:05.557
down here we've got a bit missing.

00:05:05.594 --> 00:05:07.389
It kind of looks a bit strange here.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.501
And we've got this black stroke
around it.

00:05:09.516 --> 00:05:11.529
This signifies to me it's not
big enough.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:12.609
The shape that I've used.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.113
It needs to have a bit more of a bleed, 
so we need to warp it even more.

00:05:16.152 --> 00:05:19.019
But unfortunately, we can't warp 
it when there's a mask on it.

00:05:19.044 --> 00:05:20.601
So get rid of the mask again.

00:05:20.676 --> 00:05:23.845
We're going to warp it again
and you'll see that it kind of

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.341
works pretty well.

00:05:25.416 --> 00:05:29.973
I want the warp to come slightly 
away from the actual shape here.

00:05:30.072 --> 00:05:32.185
It doesn't matter if it's like
a line like this, where it's

00:05:32.196 --> 00:05:35.425
quite a sharp line going up,
it's quite straight.

00:05:35.498 --> 00:05:38.125
But on these ones where it gets
a bit weird, we want to make

00:05:38.136 --> 00:05:40.585
sure that we have enough space
for the bleed.

00:05:40.658 --> 00:05:41.505
Press okay.

00:05:41.628 --> 00:05:44.205
Select the coffee cup again and
we'll mask it again.

00:05:44.268 --> 00:05:47.805
And you'll see that we get a
lot nicer off a curve down here.

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:50.685
Now we have another problem
happening here, too.

00:05:50.748 --> 00:05:53.949
The mask didn't fully work and that's 
because we weren't precise enough.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.805
So a way to mitigate this is go
to your brush, press B.

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:59.137
We're going to decrease the
brush size and we're going to

00:05:59.148 --> 00:06:02.823
increase the hardness to around
80, I think, and decrease the

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:03.957
brush size even more.

00:06:04.044 --> 00:06:06.421
And when we're in black and
white, we can actually change

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:08.637
what comes through here.

00:06:08.664 --> 00:06:10.557
I like to use the brush most of
the time.

00:06:10.644 --> 00:06:12.565
Some people might want to use
something different, but

00:06:12.576 --> 00:06:15.741
depending on what you're doing,
the brush is normally fine.

00:06:15.816 --> 00:06:19.873
Decrease the hardest to around
60 and in any area where it

00:06:19.884 --> 00:06:24.693
looks slightly strange, just decrease 
the brush size and change it.

00:06:24.732 --> 00:06:25.137
Mask it.

00:06:25.164 --> 00:06:28.833
This is non destructive, so we don't 
have to worry too much about it.

00:06:28.932 --> 00:06:31.533
And like so we've got a 
nice shape here already.

00:06:31.632 --> 00:06:34.177
The next thing to do is we need
to test whether our work is

00:06:34.188 --> 00:06:36.021
going to work with this or not.

00:06:36.096 --> 00:06:38.065
So what we do is we double
click, and this is what you

00:06:38.076 --> 00:06:40.153
normally do with all the mock
ups that you get from Envato.

00:06:40.164 --> 00:06:41.373
Double click.

00:06:41.412 --> 00:06:42.513
And we're going to bring in
some work.

00:06:42.552 --> 00:06:45.121
I'm going to just bring in all
my work from this part here,

00:06:45.132 --> 00:06:47.709
which is my logo with a cool
background on it.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.005
Get my logo in the middle.

00:06:49.068 --> 00:06:52.381
Now, when our work is in here and 
I press Command S to save it,

00:06:52.392 --> 00:06:55.201
you'll see that it appears
on our coffee mode.

00:06:55.226 --> 00:06:57.873
And it looks pretty strange so far.

00:06:57.972 --> 00:07:00.777
Now, the reason for this is the
warping isn't correct.

00:07:00.924 --> 00:07:03.325
Now, the way that I deal with
this, and I find it the most

00:07:03.336 --> 00:07:06.721
simplistic way when we get
these strange objects, is to

00:07:06.732 --> 00:07:09.181
again go into another warp.

00:07:09.266 --> 00:07:13.893
So I get rid of my mask again, and you 
can always put the mask on and off.

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:15.793
I like to test it as I go throughout.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.305
So get rid of the mask.

00:07:17.378 --> 00:07:18.993
Go ahead and warp it again.

00:07:19.092 --> 00:07:22.521
Now, from the middle here, we
can actually play around with it.

00:07:22.596 --> 00:07:24.673
And I like to have my logo
appear in it because it's

00:07:24.684 --> 00:07:27.793
something that I've spent a lot
of time viewing and I can see

00:07:27.804 --> 00:07:30.333
whether it's warping correctly
or not.

00:07:30.432 --> 00:07:32.715
And what I'm trying to do is
make it look like it's warping

00:07:32.726 --> 00:07:35.265
around, but not too much.

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:37.657
You can see here I'm changing
the handles.

00:07:37.814 --> 00:07:40.993
I'm going to mask it again, go
down with my brush and do some

00:07:41.004 --> 00:07:42.493
further refinements.

00:07:42.602 --> 00:07:44.397
So right there, that's looking
pretty good.

00:07:44.424 --> 00:07:47.365
But to go a step further, we
want to blend in a few more of

00:07:47.376 --> 00:07:50.005
the highlights into this
because right now, it kind of

00:07:50.016 --> 00:07:51.457
looks still a bit flat.

00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:54.805
So what we do is on our edit
page here, we're going to go

00:07:54.816 --> 00:07:56.541
into blending options.

00:07:56.676 --> 00:08:00.075
So right click blending options
and we'll get this layer style

00:08:00.086 --> 00:08:01.797
panel pop up here.

00:08:01.944 --> 00:08:05.857
Now, the Blend If function is
super important and really

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:09.387
powerful for any image editing,
especially when we're doing

00:08:09.398 --> 00:08:13.508
mockups because we have this,
this allows us to Blend If.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.905
The underlying gray is this,
it will blend it through.

00:08:16.968 --> 00:08:18.441
But you see, this doesn't look
very good.

00:08:18.516 --> 00:08:21.493
However, if we click but hold
option at the same time,

00:08:21.504 --> 00:08:22.761
it will do it like this.

00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:26.841
You'll see that it will break apart, 
but it's a lot more of a softer effect.

00:08:26.916 --> 00:08:29.989
And what we want to do is just
bring it a few more of those highlights.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:33.956
And you'll see as I do it,
those highlights just appear in.

00:08:34.044 --> 00:08:37.213
Now, we can do the same with
the blacks also, but we kind of

00:08:37.224 --> 00:08:41.677
like the blacks as well to be
in there, press okay and boom.

00:08:41.774 --> 00:08:45.253
Before I go ahead and show you
how to colour the lid off the

00:08:45.264 --> 00:08:47.641
coffee cup, I just want to tell
you about Envato because if

00:08:47.652 --> 00:08:50.473
you're watching this, you're
wanting to make mockups.

