00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.077
Okay, let's try and colour in this lid.

00:10:05.114 --> 00:10:06.013
We're going to go to Layer.

00:10:06.062 --> 00:10:10.029
We're going to go to New Fill
Layer, Solid Color and press okay.

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:13.237
I'm going to change this to
something crazy like another pink.

00:10:13.334 --> 00:10:15.057
Bring this down for now.

00:10:15.144 --> 00:10:15.393
Okay.

00:10:15.432 --> 00:10:18.025
We have a solid colour where we
can just instantly change it if

00:10:18.036 --> 00:10:20.377
we need to by double clicking
on it, which is always nice,

00:10:20.388 --> 00:10:23.953
but we need to mask everything
out again, like so I'm going to

00:10:23.964 --> 00:10:26.593
copy and paste it because it
makes life easier for myself

00:10:26.604 --> 00:10:28.298
and get rid of it there.

00:10:28.392 --> 00:10:32.085
Select change it to red so I know 
not to mess around with it too much.

00:10:32.148 --> 00:10:34.563
Now when it's selected, I'm
going to press Command Shift

00:10:34.574 --> 00:10:36.033
and I to invert it.

00:10:36.072 --> 00:10:38.073
Now we're going to bring the
field colour to the top here.

00:10:38.112 --> 00:10:41.593
I'm going to change it to Linear 
Burn again so we can see

00:10:41.604 --> 00:10:42.573
what's underneath it.

00:10:42.612 --> 00:10:45.889
I'm going to select the top of
the coffee cup again to the lid.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.745
Then I'm going to press Command
Shift and I, that's going to

00:10:48.756 --> 00:10:50.065
invert the selection.

00:10:50.138 --> 00:10:53.695
So when we click on the actual mask 
for the colour fill, the backspace

00:10:53.704 --> 00:10:57.097
it will already be on top of our mug.

00:10:57.134 --> 00:11:00.541
And we can actually change this
on the fly by going in adding

00:11:00.552 --> 00:11:02.805
or taking away with the brush
tool.

00:11:02.868 --> 00:11:04.797
But I'm going to change the
opacity of this.

00:11:04.824 --> 00:11:06.885
So we just have a little bit of
colour there.

00:11:06.948 --> 00:11:08.941
But now when we double click,
you can see that we can change

00:11:08.952 --> 00:11:12.973
the colour of this lid and it
has a metallic look to it as

00:11:12.984 --> 00:11:15.913
well, so we can change the
brightness to make it a sort of

00:11:15.924 --> 00:11:17.457
green autumnal colour.

00:11:17.544 --> 00:11:18.573
And there you have it.

00:11:18.612 --> 00:11:19.641
There is the mockup.

00:11:19.656 --> 00:11:21.093
It's fully editable as well.

00:11:21.132 --> 00:11:23.181
You can go even further than
this, actually.

00:11:23.316 --> 00:11:25.213
You can create some shadows.

00:11:25.322 --> 00:11:26.373
You can make it so you move.

00:11:26.412 --> 00:11:29.661
You can duplicate it and change 
the perspective of everything else.

00:11:29.736 --> 00:11:32.581
You can do a lot with this, but
this is the most simple way of

00:11:32.592 --> 00:11:36.865
creating a mockup onto a
coffee cup or anything else

00:11:36.876 --> 00:11:39.853
that you can think of, using
these methods and principles.

00:11:39.902 --> 00:11:41.193
This is how you do it.

